# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Staff registration passcodes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# These replace `python manage.py createsuperuser`.
#
# A new staff member opens  /accounts/register/ , picks their role, and types
# the passcode for that role. Each role has its OWN code:
#
#   PASSCODE_ADMIN    -> creates an Administrator account
#   PASSCODE_MANAGER  -> creates a Manager account
#
# CHANGE BOTH OF THESE BEFORE YOU GO LIVE. The values below are placeholders
# so the page opens on your machine - they are not secret, they are in your
# repository, and anyone who reads this file can create an admin account.
#
# What an ADMIN passcode gives away: full sight of every manager's products,
# customers, sales, debts and profit figures. Guard it like the shop keys.
#
# Notes:
#   * Blank = that role cannot register, and it disappears from the form.
#     Both blank = the whole registration page is closed. (That is what you
#     were seeing.)
#   * Wrong attempts are limited to 5 per device per 15 minutes, and every
#     attempt is written to the audit log with its IP address.
#   * Set REGISTRATION_ENABLED=False to close registration without deleting
#     the codes - useful once all your staff have accounts.
PASSCODE_ADMIN=faruqA1212
PASSCODE_MANAGER=faruqM1212
REGISTRATION_ENABLED=True